# Accessibility — WCAG 2.1 AA Rules

## Images
- All images: `alt="{{ image.alt | escape }}"` — never omit
- Decorative images: `alt=""` AND `aria-hidden="true"`
- Product images: alt should describe the product, not just say "product image"

## Interactive Elements
- Every button must have visible label text OR `aria-label="..."`
- Icon-only buttons: `<button aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.next_slide' | t }}"><svg aria-hidden="true">...</svg></button>`
- Never use `<div>` or `<span>` as clickable elements — always `<button>` or `<a>`
- Links must have descriptive text — avoid "click here" or "read more" alone
- "Read more" links: `<a href="...">{{ 'accessibility.read_more' | t: title: article.title }}</a>`

## Forms
- Every `<input>` needs a `<label>` — use `for`/`id` pairing or `aria-label`
- Required fields: add `required` attribute AND visual indicator with explanation
- Error messages: use `aria-describedby` to link errors to inputs
- Use `autocomplete` attributes on common fields (name, email, address)

## Focus Management
- Never use `outline: none` without a visible replacement
- Modals/drawers: move focus to container on open, return focus to trigger on close
- Use `tabindex="-1"` on modal wrapper, call `.focus()` programmatically
- Keyboard navigation must work for ALL interactive elements

## Dynamic Content
- Cart count updates: `<span aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">{{ cart.item_count }}</span>`
- Loading states: `aria-busy="true"` on container during async operations
- Success/error messages: `role="alert"` for immediate announcement
- Search results: announce count update with `aria-live="polite"`

## Color & Contrast
- Text contrast ratio: minimum 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text (18pt+)
- Never convey information by color alone — add text/icon/pattern
- Focus indicators: minimum 3:1 contrast against adjacent colors

## Semantic Structure
- One `<h1>` per page — typically the product/page/collection title
- Heading hierarchy: never skip levels (h1 → h2 → h3, not h1 → h3)
- Use `<nav aria-label="...">` for all navigation landmarks
- Use `<main>` wrapping the primary content — Dawn already does this
- Use `<ul>`/`<ol>` for lists — not `<div>` sequences

## Skip Links
- Dawn includes skip-to-content link — ensure it is visible on focus
- Verify `#MainContent` ID exists on the main element

## Screen Reader Utilities
- Use `.visually-hidden` (Dawn provides this class) for sr-only text
- Dawn's class: `.visually-hidden { position: absolute; clip: rect(0,0,0,0); ... }`
- Use `aria-hidden="true"` on purely decorative SVGs and icons
